{"body":"## Problem\n\n`data/ingredients/mapped/Distilled_Water.yaml` is grounded to generic\n`CHEBI:15377 water`, but its live synonym list grades materially distinct water\npreparations as `EXACT_SYNONYM`, including:\n\n- `Tap water`\n- `Double distilled water`\n- `Demineralized water`\n- `BOUND WATER`\n\nThis makes `docs/data/label_index.csv` resolve those recipe labels to the\nDistilled water record as though the supplied materials were interchangeable.\nThey are not: tap-water composition is source-dependent, demineralization and\ndistillation are different processes, double-distilled water is a distinct\npurity specification, and bound water is not a purchasable synonym for\ndistilled water.\n\nThe labels arrived through kg-microbe synonym enrichment, but ontology synonym\nscope cannot override MIM's supplied-form identity rule. The same distinction\nis now explicit in `MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md` section 3 and\n`docs/HIERARCHY_GUIDE.md` after #448.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Review every synonym on the Distilled water record against recipe-level\n  supplied-form identity.\n- Remove or retype false `EXACT_SYNONYM` assertions without losing source\n  provenance.\n- Decide whether each recipe-relevant preparation needs its own record and\n  ontology/registry/local grounding; do not collapse them merely because ChEBI\n  supplies only generic water.\n- Regenerate the label index and published exports after curation.\n- Harden synonym enrichment so broad ontology synonym imports cannot silently\n  turn distinct material grades/preparations into exact recipe-label identity.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Tap, double-distilled, demineralized, and bound water are not published as\n      exact synonyms of Distilled water unless evidence establishes literal\n      supplied-form identity.\n- [ ] All retained raw labels preserve their source/provenance.\n- [ ] Label-index resolution reflects the reviewed dispositions.\n- [ ] A regression prevents the enrichment path from recreating these false\n      exact synonyms.\n- [ ] No water/purity hierarchy is invented in MIM; any future relationship\n      model follows the stable-record contract tracked in #236/#447.\n\nRelated: #448, #232, #236, #447.\n","comments":[],"number":470,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Review false exact synonyms that collapse distinct water preparations into Distilled water","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/470"}
